hashtag textile is a celebration of the  remarkable and dynamic synergy between  contemporary fashion and technology if  you're interested in the future of  fashion and you want to think about what  may be coming down the road in terms of  how these production processes are going  to affect the making of fashion the  wearing of fashion what we've tried to  do is present that to the public so we  have a lot of technologies in there that  actually have not been employed on any  kind of mass scale but probably will be  in the future I think that what is  really fascinating about what you can do  with some of these technologies now is  this idea that it can be even more  personally expressive because you can  kind of customize it so you think about  digital printing for example there are a  number of websites already that you can  go on you can choose the images that you  want to wear on your body that's quite  amazing if you look at our cute circuit  dress that is embedded with micro LEDs  you could choose the imagery that's  going to appear on your garment and so  there is this incredible freedom of  expression this real amazing creativity  that I think you're going to be able to  achieve in the future we have quite a  few objects in the exhibition dresses  and shoes that have been made on a 3d  printer we have a dress from 2013 which  is this really beautiful cape and skirt  which is certainly wearable but it's a  slightly more conceptual piece but then  if you fast forward to two of the more  contemporary pieces we have that were  made just in the past year we have a  piece by three s4 which actually is made  out of kind of a crushable material that  you can actually  we also have a piece by nervous system  which is a Somerville based company  which is the 3d printed dress that you  can wear and you can also customise it  you can change the hemline you can  change the neckline you can change where  the petals fall as well as it's based on  a 3d scan of your body so it's going to  perfectly fit that was something  formerly reserved for a Couture client  so this idea that you can actually  access something that is custom fit to  your body is quite revolutionary yeah I  know I think that we are in an extremely  individualistic age of fashion I think  people now feel more comfortable using  fashion as a form of expression because  they have a platform a lot of that is  social media-driven  and I think that's really fascinating  and I think that a lot of what's  happening now with this customization  kind of plays into that as well I hope  that people leave feeling excited about  the future I hope that they leave having  learned something about what I think is  a very exciting synergy between the  fashion and technology worlds right now
 

